# Java String & Input-Output Notes

## 1. Input / Output in Java

### Output (Printing)

```java
System.out.println("Hello World");   // prints with new line
System.out.print("Hello");           // prints without new line
System.out.printf("Value: %d", 10);  // formatted output
```

### Input (Using Scanner)

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

int num = sc.nextInt();     // integer input
String str = sc.next();     // single word
String line = sc.nextLine();// full line
```

---

## 2. charAt() Method

### Description:

Returns character at a specific index.

### Syntax:

```java
string.charAt(index);
```

### Example:

```java
String name = "Java";
char ch = name.charAt(1); // 'a'
```

---

## 3. replace() Method

### Description:

Replaces characters or substrings.

### Syntax:

```java
string.replace(oldChar, newChar);
string.replace("old", "new");
```

### Example:

```java
String str = "hello";
String newStr = str.replace('l', 'p'); // "heppo"
```

---

## 4. substring() Method

### Description:

Extracts part of a string.

### Syntax:

```java
string.substring(startIndex);
string.substring(startIndex, endIndex);
```

### Example:

```java
String str = "Programming";

String sub1 = str.substring(3);     // "gramming"
String sub2 = str.substring(0, 6);  // "Progra"
```

